<title>USA: TSI Inc wins $7.1 mln U.S. Army contract.</title>
<headline>TSI Inc wins $7.1 mln U.S. Army contract.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PAUL, Minn. 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>TSI Inc said Tuesday the U.S. Army exercised an option to buy respirator testers, an order valued at $7.1 million.</p>
<p>TSI said the order for its Portacount Respirator Fit Testers will make a significant contribution to sales and earnings in fiscal 1998, which begins April 1, 1997.</p>
<p>Delivery of the testers will begin in March and continue for 13 months at the rate of about 100 per month, TSI said.</p>
<p>TSI manufactures measuring instruments for research and industry.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787</p>
</text>
